   "id": "astable",
   "title": "Circuit for astable operation",
   "page": 6,
   "description": "One timer as a free-running oscillator. The timing capacitor C sits on THRES and TRIG together, so it cycles between the two internal levels: it charges from VCC through RA and RB while the output is high, and discharges through RB into DISCH while the output is low. RESET is held at VCC, RL pulls the output toward VCC, and CONT is left open.",
