 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Overview",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two timers of the 555 kind share one package, a supply pin and a ground pin, and otherwise work independently. Each runs as a one-shot or an oscillator, timed by an external resistor and capacitor, over intervals from microseconds to hours. Its interval can also be steered by driving the CONT pin."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Threshold and trigger levels",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "With CONT open, each timer's threshold level is about two thirds of VCC and its trigger level about one third. A voltage applied at CONT shifts both."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input priority",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "RESET has the highest priority: low, it holds the output low with discharge on and can restart timing. Next comes TRIG: below its level, the output goes high and discharge turns off. THRES acts last: with TRIG above its level and THRES above its own, the output goes low and discharge turns on. With both inside their levels the output keeps its state."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Discharge",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "While a timer's output is low its DISCH pin offers a low-impedance path to GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each output has active pull-up and pull-down and sinks or sources up to 150 mA, with TTL-compatible levels. The recommended output current is ±200 mA and the absolute maximum ±225 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Timer matching",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Between the two timers of one package, the temperature coefficient of the timing interval differs by ±10 ppm/°C typ and the supply sensitivity by ±0.2 %/V typ (SE556 ±0.1 %/V); the initial timing error differs by ±1 typ (SE556 ±0.5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Grades",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "NE556 covers 0°C to 70°C, SA556 -40°C to 85°C, NA556 -40°C to 105°C and SE556 -55°C to 125°C. SE556 has tighter limits, an 18 V supply ceiling and a 10.6 V maximum threshold at VCC = 15 V; the others reach 11.2 V. NE556DR is the 0°C to 70°C part in the 14-pin SOIC on a 2500-piece reel."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Interchangeability",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "NE556, SA556 and SE556 replace the Signetics parts of the same numbers."
  }
 ],
